==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Condemned Peng]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Le'Behemoth]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Ange Lackey]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
**4 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**4 [[Mega Baa Baa]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Contrary to this stage's name, you will probably find yourself sleeping given the lack of any kind of pushing power present in this stage. The startoff has literally nothing besides peons and a Condemned Peng, so you can use well-timed [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cats]] to chip down the Peng, then stall for cash.

On base hit, you are greeted by Le'Behemoth and Ange Lackey. Your goal is to pierce Le'Behemoth's [[Shield]] so you can kill him quickly, using either [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] or [[Pied Piper Cat (Rare Cat)|Brass Cat]]. Once the Shield is broken, the supporting enemies will die quickly to [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]]. While Newtone doesn't seem great here given the [[Surge Attack|Surges]] and Lackey, Newtone's high range means that often he'll completely dodge the Peng's Death Surges and the Counter-Surges from Mega Baa Baa. In addition, Lackey standing behind Le'Behemoth means that their [[Explosion]] will usually miss Newtone. With [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize]] perma-stalling Le'Behemoth, it will take a miracle for the enemies to reach your Uril and Newtone. Once Le'Behemoth goes down, you've won the stage.

